### What was built

**12 nodes, 11 edges** — a decision-tree triage flow:

```
start (Manual trigger)
  └─► checkProductionDown (Decision)
        ├─ true ─► checkCriticalFlag (Decision)
        │              ├─ true (Enterprise tier OR critical impact)
        │              │    └─► classifyP1 → endP1  [P1 / immediate / engineeringNeeded=true]
        │              └─ false
        │                   └─► checkWorkaround (Decision)
        │                            ├─ true  ─► classifyP3 → endP3  [P3 / standard / engineeringNeeded=false]
        │                            └─ false ─► classifyP2 → endP2  [P2 / urgent / engineeringNeeded=depends on tier]
        └─ false ─► classifyP4 → endP4  [P4 / low / engineeringNeeded=false]
```

**Severity logic:**
| Path | severity | engineeringNeeded | responseMode |
|---|---|---|---|
| Production down + (Enterprise tier OR critical impact) | `P1` | `true` | `immediate` |
| Production down, no workaround, non-critical tier | `P2` | `true` if Enterprise | `urgent` |
| Production down, workaround available | `P3` | `false` | `standard` |
| Not production down | `P4` | `false` | `low` |

**`caseKey`** = `correlationId + "-P<n>"` on every path.

All 5 inputs (`customerTier`, `productionDown`, `workaroundAvailable`, `businessImpact`, `correlationId`) are declared as `in` variables bound to the trigger. All 4 outputs (`severity`, `engineeringNeeded`, `responseMode`, `caseKey`) are declared as `out` variables and mapped on every reachable End node.

